  "id": "Compound::DB00393 - Gene::775",
  "verbalization": "Nimodipine is likely to interact with Cacna1c through a shared pathway involving high voltage-gated calcium channels. The evidence suggests that Nimodipine binds to Cacna1f, Cacna1s, or Cacnb1, all of which participate in high voltage-gated calcium channel activity, which in turn is participated by Cacna1c. This implies that Nimodipine may modulate Cacna1c through a common mechanism involving calcium channel activity. The consistent involvement of these genes in the same functional pathway supports a potential role for Nimodipine in influencing Cacna1c function, possibly through calcium-dependent signaling. The overlapping pathways highlight a possible mechanism by which Nimodipine could affect Cacna1c, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
